From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:39:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wired-tpo for BatmanV: remove dead mesh-vpn interface

On parker the mesh VPN is handled by ffbs-mesh-vpn-parker, which creates one
plain WireGuard interface per concentrator (wg_c<id>) and routes over it at
L3. None of them is ever attached to batman-adv as a hardif, and no interface
called "mesh-vpn" exists anymore, so that arm of the condition can never
match. It is a leftover from the fastd-era single mesh-vpn hardif.

Keep vx_mesh_uplink and vx_mesh_other: Batman V still runs the local wired and
wireless mesh, and the throughput override is what makes wired links outrank
wireless ones there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../core/mesh/post-setup.d/40-gluon-mesh-batman-adv-wired-tpo   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/files/lib/gluon/core/mesh/post-setup.d/40-gluon-mesh-batman-adv-wired-tpo b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/files/lib/gluon/core/mesh/post-setup.d/40-gluon-mesh-batman-adv-wired-tpo
index caecb3dc..06ef5673 100755
--- a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/files/lib/gluon/core/mesh/post-setup.d/40-gluon-mesh-batman-adv-wired-tpo
+++ b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/files/lib/gluon/core/mesh/post-setup.d/40-gluon-mesh-batman-adv-wired-tpo
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
-if [ "$IFNAME" = "vx_mesh_uplink" ] || [ "$IFNAME" = "vx_mesh_other" ] || [ "$IFNAME" = "mesh-vpn" ]; then
+if [ "$IFNAME" = "vx_mesh_uplink" ] || [ "$IFNAME" = "vx_mesh_other" ]; then
 	sleep 3;
 	batctl hardif "${IFNAME}" throughput_override 1000mbit;
 fi
